        "id": "ch16_2_3-1",
        "text": "Enumerations\nAn enumeration is a list of constant values. While we haven\u2019t discussed them before, we have certainly used\nthem. In Chapter 10 , Error Handling \u2013 Oh No! It\u2019s Gone Wrong! , we saw the $ErrorActionPreference\nautomatic variable and how, by changing the value of the variable, we could control how PowerShell\nhandles errors temporarily. We can check the type of the $ErrorActionPreference variable\nby calling the variable GetType() method, and we can see that it is a System.Enum type in the\nfollowing screenshot:\nFigure 16.2 \u2013 How can I set thee? Let me count the ways\nWe can list out the list of possible values with the GetEnumValues() method, and we can see the\nfamiliar list of possible values. $ErrorActionPreference can only have those values, and we\ncan\u2019t change them.",
